    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_Dxy_periodic: a minimal consuming model binding NX=NY=4 at the import edge. The compound match D(D(u,x),y) fires (priority 10) through the section-9.6.3 fixpoint and lowers to the rule's makearray — the doubly-interior block [2,3]x[2,3] holding the imported 4-point centered cross-difference stencil aggregate, the four periodic-wrap edge strips (i=1, i=4 over j in [2,3]; j=1, j=4 over i in [2,3]), and the four corner cells ((1,1),(1,4),(4,1),(4,4)) that wrap both axes — with all metaparameters folded and the free names dx, dy surviving in the expanded body. The model fulfills the geometry contract with x0=y0=0 and dx=dy=1/4; the dx/dy expressions are spelled with the literal 4 because the edge binding closes NX/NY before this document's scope (grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm). The consumer writes the mixed derivative as D(D(u,x),y) (inner wrt x, outer wrt y); the golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST across bindings and confirms zero unlowered rewrite-target ops.",
